Spec: specs/002-capture-and-canonical-events/spec.md (Config: docker-compose.yml mounts a named volume and sets GATEWAY_CAPTURE_DIR; no AC)
Why this approach: follows plan.md "Docker" and the owner-accepted Dockerfile deviation. distroless has no shell, so the build stage makes an empty /out/capture and the final stage COPYs it --chown=nonroot to /var/lib/llm-gateway; Docker copies that owner onto an empty named volume. TestCompose_CaptureDirOnVolume accepts both short and long compose mount syntax and requires the source to be declared under top-level volumes (so a bind mount or anonymous volume fails). The existing stop_grace_period test now shares a readCompose helper.
Alternatives rejected: numeric --chown=65532 (the task names nonroot, which distroless's /etc/passwd resolves); a bind mount (tied to one host path, and root-owned on first use).
Trade-off / known limit: the test checks compose only; the Dockerfile ownership is proved by the manual run below, not by make verify (plan.md Risks: Docker volume ownership). docs/capture.md does not yet mention the volume (out of this task's scope).
Verified by: TestCompose_CaptureDirOnVolume (failed first with "gateway service does not set GATEWAY_CAPTURE_DIR"); docker compose config parses the file (Docker present); docker build plus a run with a fresh named volume logged "gateway started" and left gateway.db, -wal, -shm owned 65532:65532 mode 0600 in a 0700 dir (throwaway image, container and volume removed); make verify.
